---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About CompareVue"
  description="We're an independent software review site. We test tools hands-on, compare features, and help businesses make smarter buying decisions."
>
  <!-- ═══ Hero ═══ -->
  <header class="relative overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-brand-50/60 via-white to-white">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] pointer-events-none" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #2563eb 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 40px 40px;"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-14 sm:pt-20 pb-10 sm:pb-14 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <nav class="mb-6 text-sm text-gray-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
          <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600 transition-colors">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
          <li class="text-gray-500" aria-current="page">About</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl tracking-tight">About CompareVue</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg sm:text-xl text-gray-500 max-w-2xl text-pretty">We built CompareVue because choosing software shouldn't require a PhD in feature comparison.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ═══ Content ═══ -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-gray max-w-none
      prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-headings:text-gray-900
      prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-14 prose-h2:mb-5
      prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-p:text-gray-700
      prose-a:text-brand-600 prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline prose-a:font-medium
      prose-strong:text-gray-900 prose-strong:font-semibold
      prose-li:marker:text-gray-400
      prose-blockquote:border-l-4 prose-blockquote:border-brand-400 prose-blockquote:bg-brand-50/50 prose-blockquote:py-5 prose-blockquote:px-6 prose-blockquote:rounded-r-xl prose-blockquote:not-italic
    ">
      <h2>Why CompareVue Exists</h2>
      <p>We built CompareVue because <strong>choosing software sucks</strong>. Every tool promises to be "the best" — but best for who? A 5-person startup needs different things than a 500-person enterprise. A marketing team has different priorities than an engineering department.</p>

      <p>Most software review sites are either <strong>user-review free-for-alls</strong> (skewed by angry users and fake reviews) or <strong>sponsored listicles</strong> (whoever pays the most ranks highest). We wanted a third option: honest, hands-on comparisons written by people who actually test the tools.</p>

      <div class="my-10 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/50 p-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-800 mb-2">Our Promise</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-brand-700/80 leading-relaxed">Every comparison is based on real testing — we sign up, configure workflows, and use each tool for real projects. No tool company has ever paid for placement, edited our content, or influenced our verdicts. If a tool wins, it earned it.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>How We Test</h2>
      <p>We sign up for every tool we review — free trials, free plans, occasionally paid subscriptions. We test real workflows, not demos: setting up pipelines, configuring automations, managing real projects. We check support response times, mobile app quality, and the actual onboarding experience.</p>

      <p>Comparisons are updated at least every 3 months (and immediately when major pricing changes happen). We note the last updated date on every page so you know you're reading current information.</p>

      <h2>Our Rating Criteria</h2>
      <p>Every tool is evaluated across five dimensions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ease of use</strong> — How fast can a new team get productive? Is the interface intuitive or does it need training?</li>
        <li><strong>Features</strong> — Does the tool actually solve the core problem? Are features polished or checkbox items?</li>
        <li><strong>Pricing</strong> — Is the value proportional to the cost? Are there hidden costs (implementation, add-ons, admin overhead)?</li>
        <li><strong>Integrations</strong> — Does it connect to the tools your team already uses? Are integrations native or flimsy Zapier hacks?</li>
        <li><strong>Support & Reliability</strong> — What happens when something breaks? How fast is support? Is the mobile app usable?</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who's Behind CompareVue</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-5 my-8 p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 bg-white">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0">
          <div class="h-24 w-24 rounded-full bg-brand-100 flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden">
            <span class="text-3xl">👤</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Justin Guindi</h3>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-brand-600">Founder & Lead Reviewer</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Justin Guindi has been in the SaaS business for 3 years, testing and working with tools across project management, CRM, and marketing automation. He started CompareVue to cut through the noise of sponsored rankings and AI-generated listicles — building a comparison site where every tool is tested hands-on and the best product wins on merit, not ad spend.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>We're based in Europe and operate independently — no VC funding, no parent company pressure, no editorial interference from advertisers.</p>

      <h2>How We Make Money</h2>
      <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you click and buy, we may earn a commission — at no extra cost to you. This is how we pay for hosting, tool subscriptions, and the time required to maintain 59+ pages of research.</p>

      <p>Affiliate relationships never affect our ratings. We regularly recommend free tools (HubSpot's free CRM, ClickUp's free plan) and tools with no affiliate program. Our "Verdict" on every comparison page is based on testing, not commissions.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ CTA ═══ -->
    <div class="mt-16 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-600 via-brand-700 to-brand-800 p-10 sm:p-12 text-center relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10 pointer-events-none" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle, white 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 28px 28px;"></div>
      <div class="relative">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">See our work in action</h3>
        <p class="text-brand-200/90 max-w-md mx-auto">Browse our comparison library — every page is backed by real testing.</p>
        <div class="mt-6">
          <a href="/comparisons" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-white px-8 py-3.5 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700 hover:bg-brand-50 transition shadow-lg shadow-black/10">
            Browse Comparisons
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
